276
00:13:08,241 --> 00:13:10,900
If the sheet's going in the funnel, then what?

277
00:13:10,901 --> 00:13:13,940
That's an extruder, so that's gonna push the dough through.

278
00:13:13,941 --> 00:13:15,800
It's kind of like a little wheel in there.

279
00:13:15,801 --> 00:13:17,060
Think of like a mill on the river,

280
00:13:17,061 --> 00:13:18,840
turning and bringing the water around.

281
00:13:18,841 --> 00:13:21,580
So it pushes it through, and then a knife cuts it,

282
00:13:21,581 --> 00:13:24,000
and it turns into a little four-ounce slug.

283
00:13:24,001 --> 00:13:26,240
Those four-ounce chunks of Play-Doh,

284
00:13:26,241 --> 00:13:29,980
a perfect amount for young, imaginative hands,

285
00:13:29,981 --> 00:13:32,140
then need to be canned.

286
00:13:32,141 --> 00:13:33,560
So that's where all our cups are going

287
00:13:33,561 --> 00:13:34,920
to meet the dough right now.

288
00:13:34,921 --> 00:13:36,920
Amazing.

289
00:13:36,921 --> 00:13:37,920
Amazing.

290
00:13:37,921 --> 00:13:40,920
Now we're beating the cans, the dough, and the lid

291
00:13:40,921 --> 00:13:42,920
to make that full can of dough.

