00:13:42,921 --> 00:13:44,920
But the lids are loaded by hand, right?

293
00:13:44,921 --> 00:13:45,920
Yep.

294
00:13:45,921 --> 00:13:47,920
So if you take some Play-Doh home,

295
00:13:47,921 --> 00:13:49,920
and it's not getting everywhere,

296
00:13:49,921 --> 00:13:51,920
and you can put it away,

297
00:13:51,921 --> 00:13:53,920
that lid, courtesy of Gavin.

298
00:13:53,921 --> 00:13:55,920
So thank you, America.

299
00:13:55,921 --> 00:13:57,920
Do it.

300
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:03,920
And for taking this selfie,

301
00:14:03,921 --> 00:14:06,920
he gave me a surprise gift.

302
00:14:06,921 --> 00:14:09,920
It's still warm. It's still warm.

303
00:14:09,921 --> 00:14:12,920
It almost makes it more gooey and pliable.

304
00:14:12,921 --> 00:14:14,920
That is amazing.

305
00:14:14,921 --> 00:14:20,920
This was flour and pigment and salt and cornstarch

306
00:14:20,921 --> 00:14:24,920
just moments ago right up there with Troy,

307
00:14:24,921 --> 00:14:26,920
and now I can do anything with it.

308
00:14:26,921 --> 00:14:28,920
Once they're filled and capped,

309
00:14:28,921 --> 00:14:32,920
these cans of Play-Doh magic are sent through machines

310
00:14:32,921 --> 00:14:35,680
through machines that check that they each weigh

311
00:14:35,681 --> 00:14:40,240
