00:17:00,261 --> 00:17:01,260
That's all I need.

362
00:17:01,261 --> 00:17:03,060
Yeah.

363
00:17:03,061 --> 00:17:05,260
Classic toys like Play-Doh

364
00:17:05,261 --> 00:17:08,200
are blank canvases for the imagination

365
00:17:08,201 --> 00:17:11,840
to create infinite possibilities.

366
00:17:11,841 --> 00:17:15,600
But some classic toys have only one objective,

367
00:17:15,601 --> 00:17:20,140
to score big, the pinball machine.

368
00:17:20,141 --> 00:17:23,340
Over the last decade or so, interest in this classic toy

369
00:17:23,341 --> 00:17:26,740
has skyrocketed with a growing number of players

370
00:17:26,741 --> 00:17:29,440
and competitions worldwide.

371
00:17:29,441 --> 00:17:34,320
And while the demand rises, there is still only one

372
00:17:34,321 --> 00:17:37,980
manufacturer that stands high above the rest.

373
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:50,900
Now, while versions of pinball have existed since Ulysses S.

374
00:17:50,901 --> 00:17:54,100
Grant was president in the 1870s,

375
00:17:54,101 --> 00:17:58,460
Today, Stern is the world's oldest and largest manufacturer

376
00:17:58,461 --> 00:18:01,360
of arcade-quality pinball machines.

377
00:18:01,361 --> 00:18:04,160
And in recent years, Stern's revenue

378
00:18:04,161 --> 00:18:09,360
has seen year-over-year growth of up to 40%.

379
00:18:09,361 --> 00:18:12,600
Here at their 110,000-square-foot facility,

380
00:18:12,601 --> 00:18:14,800
they do it all, from designing the game

381
00:18:14,801 --> 00:18:17,140
to play testing the final product.

382
00:18:17,141 --> 00:18:20,180
Each of these machines is a work of art.

383
00:18:20,181 --> 00:18:21,740
So to find out how they've managed

384
00:18:21,741 --> 00:18:25,480
to marry cutting-edge technology with nostalgia and fun,

385
00:18:25,481 --> 00:18:30,440
I'm going to talk to the founder and CEO himself, Gary Stern,

386
00:18:30,441 --> 00:18:35,200
to find out how they have become the pinball wizards.

387
00:18:35,201 --> 00:18:37,980
My father started as a game operator in the 30s

388
00:18:37,981 --> 00:18:39,060
in Philadelphia.

389
00:18:39,061 --> 00:18:42,540
And in 1947, he came to Chicago.

390
00:18:42,541 --> 00:18:45,340
For four decades, the Stern family

391
00:18:45,341 --> 00:18:47,660
worked with another famous pinball maker,

392
00:18:47,661 --> 00:18:50,120
the Williams Company.

393
00:18:50,121 --> 00:18:55,520
And in 1986, Stern branched off into their own company,

394
00:18:55,521 --> 00:18:58,880
which Gary continues to run to this day.

395
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:05,360
PINNBALL MACHINES BECAME EXTREMELY POPULAR IN THE 1930s.

396
00:19:05,361 --> 00:19:07,400
PINNBALL MACHINES WERE BEING MADE IN CHICAGO.

397
00:19:07,401 --> 00:19:10,400
ABOUT 140 DIFFERENT COMPANIES WERE MANUFACTURING THESE.

398
00:19:10,401 --> 00:19:13,280
AND THEY EVENTUALLY GOT ASSOCIATED WITH THE CHICAGO MAFIA.

399
00:19:13,281 --> 00:19:15,680
PART OF THE ISSUE WAS THAT THEY'D SPIT OUT PAYOUTS

400
00:19:15,681 --> 00:19:17,440
FOR THE HIGH-SCORING PLAYERS,

401
00:19:17,441 --> 00:19:18,920
AND SO IT WAS CONSIDERED GAMBLING.

402
00:19:20,120 --> 00:19:29,960
In the 1940s in the US, people started to be worried about children playing pinball.

403
00:19:29,961 --> 00:19:35,360
And Fiorello LaGuardia in New York declaimed against the robbing of school children's pocket

404
00:19:35,361 --> 00:19:40,260
money that should be used for buying lunch was going to pinball, so they were banned.

405
00:19:40,261 --> 00:19:44,840
The bans on pinball didn't stop people from playing.

406
00:19:44,841 --> 00:19:50,100
Much like Prohibition, speakeasy-type play areas were established underground for pinball

407
00:19:50,101 --> 00:19:52,100
The ban that kept pinball machines underground

408
00:19:52,101 --> 00:19:55,100
was finally lifted in 1976,

409
00:19:55,101 --> 00:19:58,100
when an expert pinballer by the name of Roger Sharp,

410
00:19:58,101 --> 00:20:01,100
in front of the entire New York City Council,

411
00:20:01,101 --> 00:20:03,100
Sharp pulled the plunger on a pinball machine

412
00:20:03,101 --> 00:20:05,100
and pointed down the middle lane.

413
00:20:05,101 --> 00:20:07,100
He said that because there was skill involved,

414
00:20:07,101 --> 00:20:11,100
he knew that he could get the ball to go down the middle lane.

415
00:20:11,101 --> 00:20:15,100
He hit it on the first time, and after that, it was a 6-0 vote,

416
00:20:15,101 --> 00:20:18,100
and pinball machines were legal again.

417
00:20:18,101 --> 00:20:21,100
So that's really the one pinball game

418
00:20:21,101 --> 00:20:23,100
that made the industry possible today.

419
00:20:23,101 --> 00:20:25,100
And long after that saving,

420
00:20:25,101 --> 00:20:28,100
the demand for this classic toy continues to rise.

421
00:20:28,101 --> 00:20:35,100
New machines from Stern can run a tab between $4,000 and $10,000.

422
00:20:35,101 --> 00:20:38,100
They're using some of the latest technology

423
00:20:38,101 --> 00:20:40,100
to keep the fun of this classic toy

424
00:20:40,101 --> 00:20:43,100
both challenging and nostalgic.

425
00:20:45,100 --> 00:20:47,100
To make a pinball machine,

426
00:20:47,101 --> 00:20:52,100
Stern starts here with a piece of wood, the play field.

427
00:20:52,600 --> 00:20:55,320
Stern veteran Kenny will show us how it's done.

428
00:20:56,020 --> 00:20:58,600
Basically, we start with a two-by-four piece of plywood.

429
00:20:58,940 --> 00:21:02,720
We take it over to our CNC machines that are, you know, programmed,

430
00:21:03,060 --> 00:21:04,000
and this is the output.

431
00:21:04,460 --> 00:21:08,560
So this thing makes every cut that will be on the play field in one pass.

432
00:21:08,740 --> 00:21:12,820
Your ramps, your ball guides, light fixtures, your inserts.

433
00:21:13,220 --> 00:21:14,660
My holes are off a little bit.

434
00:21:15,300 --> 00:21:16,120
It's never going to work.

435
00:21:16,121 --> 00:21:16,840
I see.

436
00:21:16,841 --> 00:21:21,520
so you have to treat these two by four pieces of plywood

437
00:21:21,521 --> 00:21:23,020
with the utmost precision.

438
00:21:23,021 --> 00:21:23,920
Absolutely.

439
00:21:23,921 --> 00:21:28,680
If the slightest angle or hole is off during this process,

440
00:21:28,681 --> 00:21:31,980
the entire gameplay experience and assembly

441
00:21:31,981 --> 00:21:34,060
could be compromised.

442
00:21:34,061 --> 00:21:38,300
After a board has been precisely cut and sanded smooth,

443
00:21:38,301 --> 00:21:40,760
the inserts are installed.

444
00:21:40,761 --> 00:21:43,760
These are the colored coverings that illuminate

445
00:21:43,761 --> 00:21:47,100
once the lights have been connected under the board.

446
00:21:47,101 --> 00:21:49,100
This is a play field that we routed over there.

447
00:21:49,101 --> 00:21:51,600
It's all cleaned up, all smooth, ready to be inserted.

448
00:21:51,601 --> 00:21:54,500
These here are the inserts that we use.

